<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Hris.Application
    Sprint 3 (Core Kernel) scope, per IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md Phase 1.
    Source specifications: docs/02-architecture/03-application-architecture/application-pipeline.md
    ("Pipeline Behaviors... Logging, Performance Monitoring, Authorization, Validation,
    Transaction, Handler, Domain Events") and docs/08-devops/coding-standards.md's
    Application Layer conventions.

    Built now, ahead of any one framework's own Application layer, because
    Hris.Foundation.Configuration's Application layer (the first Sprint 3 framework to
    need one, per IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md's bootstrap order) cannot dispatch a command
    that persists anything without it: application-pipeline.md's Transaction Behavior
    ("Begin transaction, Execute handler, Save changes, Commit transaction") and
    Common Anti-Patterns ("Manual transaction management in handlers") together mean a
    handler must never call SaveChanges itself -- that has to live in a shared pipeline
    behavior every framework's and module's commands go through identically, not
    something Configuration Framework's own Application layer would own privately.

    Depends only on Hris.SharedKernel and MediatR/FluentValidation -- never on
    Hris.Infrastructure or Entity Framework Core. <see cref="Abstractions.IUnitOfWork"/>
    is the abstraction that keeps the dependency direction correct: Application defines
    the interface a persistence concern must satisfy, Infrastructure (which references
    Application, never the reverse) provides it via HrisDbContext. Coding-standards.md
    states this rule explicitly for the Domain layer only ("Domain code has no
    reference to Entity Framework Core... CTR-ARC-001"); this project extends the same
    reasoning one layer up for Clean Architecture's inward dependency rule to hold
    end-to-end, not because CTR-ARC-001 itself names the Application layer.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Hris.Application</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Hris.SharedKernel\Hris.SharedKernel.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" Version="12.4.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" Version="11.11.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
